/-!
# Two movers, both large: the arrangement statement (GENERATED by `s2_gen_lean_all_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-22.  New file.  Speeds `c + i` (`i = 0..7`), runner `m1` at `x1`, runner `m2` at `x2` (`m1 ≠ m2`), subject `k`
not a mover.  The subject's frozen disparities `Sdisp2 k m1 m2` are one of 37 sets (`Sdisp2_cases`, by `decide`).  For each,
`landing_twoMover_<set>`: if both movers' disparities `d1 = |x1 - (c + k)|`, `d2 = |x2 - (c + k)|` are at least the threshold
`D0 = ⌈7/(4L)⌉` of that set (`L` the width of its first wide frozen piece), the first lonely instant `T` exists, is at least
`1/(8a)`, and the cascade from `1/(8a)` reaches a fixed point and every fixed point it reaches is `T`.  The finer description
of `T` (a listed point at which both movers are clear, or the first common clear instant in the wide piece) is
`land2G<set>`.  Grades: [L]; [PROVISIONAL: covering] and [PROVISIONAL: counting tool] by inheritance.  NOT covered: movers
below the threshold, one mover small, the subject among the movers.
-/

open Classical

